{"qid": "tsunami-wait-ja", "event": "answer", "q": "海の近くで強い揺れを感じました。津波警報はまだ出ていません。警報が出るまで待ってから逃げればいいですか？", "lang": "ja", "alerts": ["tsunami-go-high"], "retrieved": [{"id": 40, "source": "kantei-tsunami", "score": 0.0338, "cos": 0.811}, {"id": 42, "source": "kantei-tsunami", "score": 0.0338, "cos": 0.779}, {"id": 37, "source": "kantei-tsunami", "score": 0.0333, "cos": 0.765}, {"id": 47, "source": "kantei-tsunami", "score": 0.0324, "cos": 0.766}], "a": "強い揺れを感じた場合は、津波警報が出ていなくてもすぐに避難を開始すべきです[2]。海岸付近にいる人は、「津波注意報」でも避難が必要であり、海からあがるなどすぐに避難を始める必要があります[1]。", "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 1464, "total_ms": 2247, "input_tokens": 1055, "output_tokens": 54, "tokens_per_s": 67.7, "rss_mb": 5290}
{"qid": "tsunami-wait-en", "event": "answer", "q": "I felt strong shaking near the beach. There is no tsunami warning yet. Should I wait for the warning before I leave?", "lang": "en", "alerts": ["tsunami-go-high"], "retrieved": [{"id": 40, "source": "kantei-tsunami", "score": 0.0172, "cos": 0.734}, {"id": 134, "source": "jma-sekiranun-hinan", "score": 0.0169, "cos": 0.721}, {"id": 41, "source": "kantei-tsunami", "score": 0.0166, "cos": 0.7}, {"id": 25, "source": "kantei-jishin", "score": 0.0163, "cos": 0.699}], "a": "If you feel strong shaking, you should leave the coast as quickly as possible and evacuate to the highest place you can [1]. People near the coast need to evacuate even for a \"tsunami advisory\" [1]. When evacuating, go to nearby high ground, a tsunami evacuation tower, or a tsunami evacuation building [1].", "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 826, "total_ms": 1720, "input_tokens": 975, "output_tokens": 68, "tokens_per_s": 75.0, "rss_mb": 5295}
{"qid": "snakebite-tie-ja", "event": "answer", "q": "腕をマムシに噛まれました。毒が回らないように、噛まれた所の上をひもできつく縛ったほうがいいですか？", "lang": "ja", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 177, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0333, "cos": 0.765}, {"id": 178, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0325, "cos": 0.756}, {"id": 176, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0313, "cos": 0.737}, {"id": 179, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0311, "cos": 0.737}], "a": "氷を当てたり止血帯を使ったりすることは、効果がなくさらに害を与える可能性があるため避けてください [2]。かまれた部分の上に滅菌された包帯または被覆材をぴったりと当てますが、きつく締めすぎないようにしてください [2]。毒が広がるのを遅らせるために、可能であればかまれた手足を心臓の高さより少し低くすることが役立つことがあります [1]。", "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 744, "total_ms": 1852, "input_tokens": 884, "output_tokens": 84, "tokens_per_s": 74.9, "rss_mb": 5295}
{"qid": "snakebite-tie-en", "event": "answer", "q": "A snake bit my arm. Should I tie a cord tightly above the bite so the venom doesn't spread?", "lang": "en", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 177, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0167, "cos": 0.769}, {"id": 178, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0164, "cos": 0.762}, {"id": 176, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0161, "cos": 0.751}, {"id": 179, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0159, "cos": 0.746}], "a": "Do not use a TQ [2]. Apply a sterile bandage over the bite that is snug but not too tight to help immobilize the area and reduce venom spread [2]. Keep the bitten person as still and calm as possible by restricting movement [1].", "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 647, "total_ms": 1352, "input_tokens": 748, "output_tokens": 52, "tokens_per_s": 72.3, "rss_mb": 5213}
{"qid": "avalanche-buried-ja", "event": "answer", "q": "バックカントリーで仲間が雪崩に埋まりました。まず麓まで助けを呼びに行くべきですか？", "lang": "ja", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 81, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0343, "cos": 0.772}, {"id": 74, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0335, "cos": 0.746}, {"id": 129, "source": "npa-sounan-gaikyou-r07", "score": 0.0332, "cos": 0.738}, {"id": 69, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0317, "cos": 0.706}], "a": "雪崩が発生した場合は、流されている人を見続け、遭難点と消失点を覚えておく必要があります [1]。すぐに雪崩ビーコンなどを用いて捜索し、見つかれば掘り起こして救急処置を行うべきです [1]。", "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 974, "total_ms": 1695, "input_tokens": 1127, "output_tokens": 53, "tokens_per_s": 72.1, "rss_mb": 5270}
{"qid": "avalanche-buried-en", "event": "answer", "q": "A friend was buried by an avalanche in the backcountry. Should we go down to get help first?", "lang": "en", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 81, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0172, "cos": 0.737}, {"id": 73, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0169, "cos": 0.721}, {"id": 74, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0166, "cos": 0.72}, {"id": 76, "source": "kantei-setsugai", "score": 0.0163, "cos": 0.718}], "a": "If you are near an avalanche, keep watching the person being carried away [1]. After the avalanche stops, post a lookout and put markers at the accident point and disappearance point [1]. Search immediately using avalanche beacons or similar devices [1].", "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 1124, "total_ms": 1806, "input_tokens": 1258, "output_tokens": 49, "tokens_per_s": 70.4, "rss_mb": 5274}
{"qid": "heat-stroke-ja", "event": "answer", "q": "暑い日の登山中、仲間の受け答えがおかしく、汗が止まって体がとても熱いです。日陰で水を飲ませて休ませれば大丈夫ですか？", "lang": "ja", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 202, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0318, "cos": 0.713}, {"id": 193, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0292, "cos": 0.714}, {"id": 256, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0285, "cos": 0.725}, {"id": 204, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.028, "cos": 0.702}], "a": "お仲間は、大量の汗や脱力感と疲労、めまいなどの症状がある場合、熱疲労の兆候である可能性があります [2]。体温が高く、受け答えがおかしい場合は熱中症（熱射病）の可能性も考慮し、冷たい水を入れた浴槽に浸す、氷の冷却シートを使う、ぬらしたタオルやスポンジで体に冷たい水をかけるなどの方法があります [1]。バイタルサインを観察し、必要に応じて心肺蘇生を行う必要があります [1]。", "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 701, "total_ms": 2138, "input_tokens": 830, "output_tokens": 111, "tokens_per_s": 76.5, "rss_mb": 5239}
{"qid": "heat-stroke-en", "event": "answer", "q": "On a hot hike my friend is confused, has stopped sweating and feels very hot. Is it enough to rest in the shade and drink water?", "lang": "en", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 195, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0167, "cos": 0.718}, {"id": 204, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0164, "cos": 0.707}, {"id": 193, "source": "army-atp-4-02-11", "score": 0.0161, "cos": 0.706}, {"id": 257, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0159, "cos": 0.705}], "a": "You should understand the signs of heat stroke and promptly seek medical help as this can save lives [2]. For heat exhaustion, you should have the person lie down and elevate their legs slightly while sipping cool water or an electrolyte-containing sports drink [1]. If they are experiencing symptoms like red skin, it indicates a severe condition requiring immediate evacuation [4].", "cited": [1, 2, 4], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 630, "total_ms": 1561, "input_tokens": 716, "output_tokens": 71, "tokens_per_s": 75.2, "rss_mb": 5240}
{"qid": "hypothermia-ja", "event": "answer", "q": "雨に濡れた仲間の震えが止まらず、ぼんやりしています。手足を強くこすって温めればいいですか？", "lang": "ja", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 251, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0315, "cos": 0.729}, {"id": 250, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0292, "cos": 0.725}, {"id": 230, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0286, "cos": 0.741}, {"id": 231, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0283, "cos": 0.743}], "a": "凍傷の手当として、患部をマッサージしたり直火に当てたりして温めてはいけません [2]。本人は暖かく風雨をしのげる場所へ移してください [2]。足が冷たい場合は、素足を仲間の衣服の下におなかに当てるなどの手当てがあります [1]。", "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 784, "total_ms": 1653, "input_tokens": 847, "output_tokens": 66, "tokens_per_s": 74.8, "rss_mb": 5239}
{"qid": "hypothermia-en", "event": "answer", "q": "My friend got soaked in the rain, can't stop shivering and seems dazed. Should I rub their arms and legs hard to warm them?", "lang": "en", "alerts": [], "retrieved": [{"id": 258, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0167, "cos": 0.715}, {"id": 251, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0164, "cos": 0.712}, {"id": 252, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0161, "cos": 0.711}, {"id": 250, "source": "army-tc-21-3", "score": 0.0159, "cos": 0.71}], "a": "Do not rub the frostbitten area with snow or apply cold water soaks [4]. You should also not rewarm the affected area by massaging or exposing it to open fire [4]. Loosening tight clothing and improving circulation by exercising are recommended actions for frostbite treatment [3].", "cited": [3, 4], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 628, "total_ms": 1423, "input_tokens": 708, "output_tokens": 59, "tokens_per_s": 73.0, "rss_mb": 5239}
